# drivers/gpu/conf: the GPU.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver ADRENO
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.adreno.c
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.adreno.sdm845.c
	file    iokit/Kernel/hakios.gpu.cpp iokitcpp
	help    the Redwood Adreno 642L rendering backend (gpu=1), the shared HakiosGPU service, and read-only Polaris Adreno 630
	help    probes (adreno=1..4), firmware/DT checks (adreno=5), read-only PAS queries (adreno=6),
	help    and explicit PAS ZAP metadata/segment staging plus shutdown (adreno=7; requires CX/GX).
	help    Polaris rendering is not enabled yet; both devices need their own firmware in fw-gpu/.
